window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d8e7ab2e8f18b498"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"site-tools\">网站工具（Site tools）</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面网址末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>Site tools（网站工具）是 ChatGPT 对拟议中的 <a href=\"https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP 标准（需联网）</a>的实现。简单说，WebMCP 让网站把预先定义的操作提供给 AI 智能体；你和智能体可以在同一个实时页面及已登录会话中协作。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用的<a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">内置浏览器</a>中，如果网站提供了网站工具，ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 就可以发现并使用这些工具。</p> <p>使用网站工具时，请选用 GPT-5.6 Sol 或 GPT-6 Sol。目前，GPT-5.6 Luna 已禁用 WebMCP。请将 ChatGPT 桌面应用更新到最新版本。在 Enterprise 工作区中，管理员必须通过工作区策略允许使用 <strong>Site tools（网站工具）</strong>。Edu 工作区不提供网站工具。是否可用也取决于功能发布进度以及当前页面提供的工具。</p> <p><a id=\"webmcp-vs-mcp\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"webmcp-mcp\">WebMCP 与 MCP 的区别</h2> <p><a href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/learn/architecture\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Model Context Protocol（模型上下文协议，MCP）（需联网）</a>将 AI 应用连接到本地或远程服务器。即使没有打开网页，MCP 工具也可以独立工作，例如搜索某项服务或通过 API 管理记录。</p> <p><a href=\"https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP（需联网）</a> 则让网站以一组预先定义的工具形式，向智能体提供自身功能。智能体访问网站时可以发现这些工具，因此用户不必另行安装 MCP 服务器或配置另一种连接，就能使用这些功能。</p> <p>如果你和智能体需要查看同一内容，这种方式会很有用，例如共同编辑画布或查看仪表板。<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">带有 MCP 服务器的插件</a>则可以提供不依赖已打开网页的集成。一个网站也可以同时支持这两种方式。</p> <p><a id=\"how-it-works-in-the-browser\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">在浏览器中的工作方式</h2> <p>在内置浏览器中打开网站，然后请 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 帮你完成任务。如果页面提供网站工具，智能体就可以发现并使用当前网站中的相关操作。例如，文档编辑器可以让智能体查找某个章节，或留下评论供你审核。</p> <p>在浏览器地址栏中选择 <strong>Site tools（网站工具）</strong>，即可查看网站提供的工具。选择 <strong>Available site tools（可用的网站工具）</strong>可查看每个工具的详情。网站执行操作前，浏览器会检查每项请求；操作后，智能体可以检查页面，确认发生了哪些变化。如果有近期活动记录，可以选择 <strong>Recently used（最近使用）</strong>，打开 <strong>Sources（来源）</strong>并查看这些调用。</p> <p>在下面的示例中，展开 <strong>Available site tools</strong>，即可查看 <a href=\"https://margin-local-docs.openai.chatgpt.site\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Margin（需联网）</a> 提供的工具。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 内置浏览器中的 Site tools 菜单，显示有 10 个可用工具。</p> </blockquote> <p>工具属于提供它们的页面。关闭页面或离开页面后，这些工具可能就无法继续使用。如果没有合适的工具，智能体仍可能使用常规浏览器功能。</p> <p><a id=\"example-explore-openai-documentation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"openai\">示例：探索 OpenAI 文档</h2> <p>ChatGPT Learn 和 OpenAI Developers 提供了查找、阅读文档的网站工具。在撰写框中选择 <strong>Open in ChatGPT（在 ChatGPT 中打开）</strong>，即可在桌面应用的浏览器中打开 Learn；它会显示在新聊天旁边，并预先填入下面的提示词。</p> <p><strong>提示词（英文原文，可直接复制）：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Find the documentation for building reusable skills, open the relevant page, and explain when I should turn a skill into a plugin.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">找到有关构建可复用技能的文档，打开相关页面，并解释我应该在什么情况下将技能转为插件。</div></div> <p>这句话的意思是：“查找有关构建可复用技能的文档，打开相关页面，并说明什么情况下应该把技能改为插件。”</p> <p>智能体可以使用下列工具搜索、读取并打开相应文档：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>工具</th> <th>作用</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>search_openai_docs</code></td> <td>搜索 OpenAI 文档。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>lookup_page</code></td> <td>根据路径或网址读取文档页面。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>lookup_context</code></td> <td>读取当前文档路由和所选文本。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>navigate_to_page</code></td> <td>在当前文档网站中打开匹配的页面。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>generate_custom_guide</code></td> <td>异步启动自定义构建或学习指南，并返回其状态和链接。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Docs Agent 会异步生成自定义指南。收到指南链接，并不表示生成过程已经完成。</p> <p><a id=\"security-and-user-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">安全与用户控制</h2> <p>网站提供的工具定义及其结果都应视为不可信内容。工具名称或其声称“只读取数据”，都不能证明它实际执行的操作是什么。网站中的说明不会授权智能体分享无关信息或采取敏感操作。</p> <p>在内置浏览器中，每次调用工具前都会经过安全检查。常规的网站访问和确认规则仍然适用，包括发送消息、购物、删除数据或更改权限等有实质影响的操作。浏览器会将每次调用关联到发起调用的页面和工具注册信息。这些检查可以降低风险，但不能让网站或其输出变得可信。</p> <p>你可以在 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Browser（浏览器）&gt; Permissions（权限）</strong>中关闭 <strong>Enable site tools（启用网站工具）</strong>。分享敏感信息或依赖某项变更前，请先检查网站、请求执行的操作和操作结果。</p> <p>安全漏洞请通过 OpenAI 的 <a href=\"https://bugcrowd.com/engagements/openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Security Bug Bounty 计划（需联网）</a>报告。AI 安全风险请通过 <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/safety-bug-bounty/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Safety Bug Bounty 计划（需联网）</a>报告。请遵守各计划的适用范围和提交说明。</p> <p><a id=\"limitations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">限制</h2> <p>ChatGPT 内置浏览器目前仅支持部分 WebMCP API，暂不支持以下功能：</p> <ul> <li><strong>声明式 API：</strong> 通过 HTML 表单属性定义的工具不会作为网站工具提供。</li> <li><strong>iframe 中的工具：</strong> 浏览器不会发现注册在 iframe 中的工具，包括同源和跨源 iframe。</li> </ul> <p>请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-d8e7ab2e8f18b498?anchor=add-webmcp-to-your-website\">下一节</a>中的示例，在顶层页面中使用 JavaScript 注册工具。ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 仍可能通过常规浏览器功能与表单交互，但这些交互不属于 WebMCP 工具调用。</p> <p>WebMCP 规范和 Chrome 开发者指南介绍了更广泛的 API，其中包括当前内置浏览器尚不支持的功能。</p> <p><a id=\"add-webmcp-to-your-website\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"webmcp\">为你的网站添加 WebMCP</h2> <p>你可以请 Codex 为正在开发的 Web 应用或 <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Site</a> 添加 WebMCP 支持。描述你希望智能体能够执行哪些操作，并请 Codex 复用应用现有的业务逻辑和权限机制。</p> <p>先从应用已经支持的操作开始。例如：</p> <ul> <li>仪表板可以让智能体设置日期范围，并查看图表背后的数据。</li> <li>文档编辑器可以让智能体查找某个章节、提出修改建议，或留下评论供你审核。</li> <li>旅行规划器可以让智能体比较选项、更新行程，同时让你查看地图。</li> </ul> <p>你也可以自行编写代码。在页面的 JavaScript 模块中，先检查浏览器是否支持，再注册工具。下面这个只读示例会返回当前页面的标题：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">if (typeof document.modelContext?.registerTool === \"function\") {\n  await document.modelContext.registerTool({\n    name: \"get_page_title\",\n    description: \"Read the title of the current page.\",\n    inputSchema: {\n      type: \"object\",\n      properties: {},\n      additionalProperties: false,\n    },\n    annotations: { readOnlyHint: true },\n    execute: async () =&gt; ({ title: document.title }),\n  });\n}\n</code></pre> <p>兼容的智能体可以发现 <code>get_page_title</code>，并获取当前页面的标题。如果要注册一个接收参数的工具，请在输入架构中描述参数，并在 <code>execute</code> 处理函数中使用这些参数调用应用现有逻辑。</p> <p>请限制输入范围、说明副作用，并返回足够的信息以便核实操作结果。使用应用现有的身份验证、授权和输入验证机制。对于不支持 WebMCP 的用户和浏览器，应继续保留正常的网站界面。</p> <p>API 详情和示例请参阅 <a href=\"https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP 规范（需联网）</a>和 <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chrome 开发者指南（需联网）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"site-tools\">Site tools</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Site tools are ChatGPT's implementation of the proposed <a href=\"https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP standard (online)</a>. With WebMCP, a website can offer useful actions directly to an AI agent alongside the interface people already use. You and the agent can work with the same live page and signed-in session.</p> <p>In the <a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">built-in browser</a> in the ChatGPT desktop app, ChatGPT Work and Codex can discover and use these tools when they are available.</p> <p>Use GPT-5.6 Sol or GPT-6 Sol for site tools. GPT-5.6 Luna currently has WebMCP disabled. Update the ChatGPT desktop app to the latest version. In Enterprise workspaces, an admin must allow <strong>Site tools</strong> through workspace policy. Site tools aren't available in Edu workspaces. Availability also depends on rollout and the tools provided by the current page.</p> <h2 id=\"webmcp-vs-mcp\">WebMCP vs. MCP</h2> <p><a href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/learn/architecture\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Model Context Protocol (MCP) (online)</a> connects an AI application to a local or remote server. Its tools can work independently of an open webpage, such as searching a service or managing records through an API.</p> <p><a href=\"https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP (online)</a> lets a website make its capabilities available to an agent as a set of predefined tools. The agent can discover them when it visits, so people don't need to install a separate MCP server or set up another connection to use those capabilities.</p> <p>This approach is useful when you and the agent need to see the same thing, such as when editing a canvas or exploring a dashboard. A <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugin with an MCP server</a> can provide an integration that works independently of an open page. A website can support both.</p> <h2 id=\"how-it-works-in-the-browser\">How it works in the browser</h2> <p>Open a website in the built-in browser and ask ChatGPT Work or Codex to help with a task. If the page offers site tools, the agent can discover and use the relevant actions in the website you're viewing. For example, a document editor might let the agent find a section or leave a comment for you to review.</p> <p>Select <strong>Site tools</strong> in the browser's address bar to see what the website provides. Choose <strong>Available site tools</strong> to inspect the individual tools. The browser checks each request before the website carries it out, and the agent can inspect the page to see what changed. When recent activity is available, choose <strong>Recently used</strong> to open <strong>Sources</strong> and review those calls.</p> <p>In this example, expand <strong>Available site tools</strong> to inspect the tools provided by <a href=\"https://margin-local-docs.openai.chatgpt.site\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Margin (online)</a>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT's built-in browser showing the Site tools menu for Margin, with 10 available tools.</p> </blockquote> <p>Tools belong to the page that provides them. Closing or navigating away from a page can make its tools unavailable. If no suitable tool is available, the agent may still be able to use its regular browser capabilities.</p> <h2 id=\"example-explore-openai-documentation\">Example: Explore OpenAI documentation</h2> <p>ChatGPT Learn and OpenAI Developers offer site tools for finding and reading documentation. Select <strong>Open in ChatGPT</strong> in the composer to open Learn in the desktop app's browser beside a new chat with this prompt ready to send.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Find the documentation for building reusable skills, open the relevant page, and explain when I should turn a skill into a plugin.\n</code></pre> <p>The agent can use these tools to search, read, and open the relevant page:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Tool</th> <th>What it does</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>search_openai_docs</code></td> <td>Searches OpenAI documentation.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>lookup_page</code></td> <td>Reads a documentation page by path or URL.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>lookup_context</code></td> <td>Reads the current docs route and selected text.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>navigate_to_page</code></td> <td>Opens a matching page on the current documentation site.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>generate_custom_guide</code></td> <td>Starts a custom build or learning guide and returns its status and link.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Docs Agent generates a custom guide asynchronously. Receiving its link doesn't mean generation has finished.</p> <h2 id=\"security-and-user-controls\">Security and user controls</h2> <p>Website-provided tool definitions and results are untrusted content. A tool's name or claim that it only reads data isn't proof of what it does. Website instructions don't give the agent permission to share unrelated information or take sensitive actions.</p> <p>In the built-in browser, each tool invocation receives a safety review before it runs. Normal website-access and confirmation policies still apply, including for consequential actions such as sending messages, making purchases, deleting data, or changing permissions. The browser ties each invocation to its originating page and tool registration. These checks reduce risk; they don't make a website or its output trustworthy.</p> <p>You can turn off <strong>Enable site tools</strong> in <strong>Settings &gt; Browser &gt; Permissions</strong>. Review the site, requested action, and result before sharing sensitive information or relying on a change.</p> <p>Report security vulnerabilities through OpenAI's <a href=\"https://bugcrowd.com/engagements/openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Security Bug Bounty program (online)</a>. For AI safety risks, see the <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/safety-bug-bounty/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Safety Bug Bounty program (online)</a>. Follow each program's scope and submission instructions.</p> <h2 id=\"limitations\">Limitations</h2> <p>ChatGPT's built-in browser currently supports a subset of the WebMCP APIs. The following features aren't supported:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Declarative API:</strong> Tools defined through HTML form attributes aren't available as site tools.</li> <li><strong>Tools in iframes:</strong> The browser doesn't discover tools registered inside iframes, including same-origin and cross-origin iframes.</li> </ul> <p>Use JavaScript to register tools in the top-level page, as shown in the <a href=\"#/article/a-d8e7ab2e8f18b498?anchor=add-webmcp-to-your-website\">next section</a>. ChatGPT Work and Codex may still interact with forms using regular browser capabilities, but those interactions aren't WebMCP tool calls.</p> <p>The WebMCP specification and Chrome's developer guide describe the broader APIs, including features that aren't currently supported in the built-in browser.</p> <h2 id=\"add-webmcp-to-your-website\">Add WebMCP to your website</h2> <p>You can ask Codex to add WebMCP support to the web app or <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Site</a> you're working on. Describe what an agent should be able to do, and ask Codex to reuse the application's existing logic and permissions.</p> <p>Start with an operation your application already supports. For example:</p> <ul> <li>A dashboard that lets the agent set a date range and inspect the data behind a chart.</li> <li>A document editor that lets the agent find a section, suggest an edit, or leave a comment for you to review.</li> <li>A travel planner that lets the agent compare options and update an itinerary while you inspect the map.</li> </ul> <p>You can also write the code yourself. In your page's JavaScript module, check for browser support and register a tool. This read-only example returns the current page's title:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">if (typeof document.modelContext?.registerTool === \"function\") {\n  await document.modelContext.registerTool({\n    name: \"get_page_title\",\n    description: \"Read the title of the current page.\",\n    inputSchema: {\n      type: \"object\",\n      properties: {},\n      additionalProperties: false,\n    },\n    annotations: { readOnlyHint: true },\n    execute: async () =&gt; ({ title: document.title }),\n  });\n}\n</code></pre> <p>A compatible agent can discover <code>get_page_title</code> and receive the page's current title. For a tool that accepts arguments, describe them in the input schema and use them in the <code>execute</code> handler to call your application's existing logic.</p> <p>Keep inputs narrow, describe side effects, and return enough information to verify the result. Use your application's existing authentication, authorization, and input validation. Preserve the normal interface for people and browsers that don't support WebMCP.</p> <p>For API details and examples, see the <a href=\"https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP specification (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chrome's developer guide (online)</a>.</p>"};
